# rule.always.razor-the-foundation-from-the-application

> **split each lesson, cure, or claim into its foundation (the law in any domain) and its application (the one act it owes here), before it lands.** miss the foundation → overspecialized. miss the application → overgeneralized.

questions: what law holds with no word of today's domain? · what one act does it owe here? · is that law already held by some role? · foundation lands in the general role, application in its domain's role and cites the foundation. where a cure lands: `skepticize-the-layer-of-a-cure`.
pair: foundation: cure the root of roots, a refusal is never the cure · application: lost bandwidth cured by per-unit cost, never fewer crews.
test: **can I state this lesson with no word of today's domain, and the one act it owes here?**
nitpick: a lesson landed with no foundation named · a lesson landed with no concrete application · a new foundation that restates an extant law
